+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+ OR MIT
+/*
+ * J604 power-domain ownership, in the form of t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi.
+ *
+ * Only the domains whose Linux power/reset contract is qualified are enabled.
+ * Retained core, GPIO and display domains are firmware-owned: neither state
+ * reads nor power/reset writes are permitted. Other domains stay unavailable
+ * until their consumer and power sequence are implemented.
+ *
+ * Each domain takes the J713 decision, except in two cases:
+ * - A domain that an enabled J604 node consumes, directly or as the parent
+ *   of a consumed domain, stays enabled. This covers ATC3 USB, the
+ *   general-purpose PCIe and the NUB SPMI buses.
+ * - The DisplayPort-out domains (dispext0/1 sys, fe, cpu), which the J713
+ *   keeps firmware-owned, are disabled here. They are off when the J604
+ *   boots and no J604 node consumes them.
+ *
+ * As on the J713, ps_pmc is not registered: the PMP firmware owns the PMC
+ * and votes in it from its first steps (see the &pmc node). ps_gfx is
+ * enabled with its gfx_tvm parent by t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi.
+ */
+
